  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "If $\\text{E}[X]=3$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=11,$ then what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$",
  "worked_solution": "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =11-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =11-9 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
